'' A SHARED OR STATIC INITIALISER THAT NAMES SOMETHING was not folded, and the two
'' halves of that failed differently.
''
'' 'dim shared b as boolean = true' got NO INITIALISER: the constant evaluator was
'' called without the symbol table, so an identifier was simply not constant here. That
'' is not a decline but a WRONG VALUE -- the global read FALSE -- and it verified.
'' fbcunit.bas declares three of its own flags that way.
''
'' 'static f as any ptr = procptr( s )' and the 'cptr( any ptr, @s )' spelling declined
'' outright: only the bare '@s' was recognised as a relocation, so the pointer was left
'' NULL. dim/static-const-init.bas writes four.
''
'' NOT MATCHED, deliberately: tiko-lang stores -1 where fbc stores 1 for a boolean TRUE.
'' Its own conversions normalise to -1 on the way out -- measured, fbc's 'print cbyte(a)'
'' over a true boolean prints -1 as well -- so nothing tiko-lang emits can tell them
'' apart, and the LOCAL path already stored -1. Making the global disagree with the
'' local would be the worse answer.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/static-init-reloc.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var ptr T$f = S
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var ptr T$g = S
'' EXPECT-OUT: global var i8 bt = -1
'' GOLDEN: expected/static-init-reloc.out
